// bubbler profile: alacritty
//
// A display, and nothing else. Alacritty draws through OpenGL and finds
// no render node in this sandbox, so it renders in software and says so
// on startup (`libEGL warning: failed to get driver name for fd -1`);
// `dri` below is what stops that.
//
// No nested user namespaces: a terminal's own sandbox has no need of one.
// The shell inside cannot start bwrap, podman or a browser's inner sandbox;
// drop the `userns` line for a terminal that hosts those.
// Bare by design. Add:
//   dri
//     — the GPU, and with it hardware glyph rendering instead of
//       llvmpipe.
wayland
userns "disable"
desktop "Alacritty.desktop"
command "alacritty"
